A Surrogate means a substitute or replacement for something else.

General Meaning

A surrogate is a person or thing that acts on behalf of another.

1️⃣ In Databases (Common in interviews)

A Surrogate Key is an artificial key created by the database to uniquely identify a row.

Example:

ID (Surrogate Key)	Name	Email
1	Ali	ali@email.com

2	Ahmed	ahmed@email.com

Here ID is a surrogate key because:

It has no business meaning

It is generated by the system (AUTO_INCREMENT)

Example SQL

CREATE TABLE users (
    id INT AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,
    name VARCHAR(50),
    email VARCHAR(50)
);

✔ id = Surrogate Key
✔ Used only for unique identification

Opposite:
Natural Key (like CNIC, email, etc.)

2️⃣ In Cloud / Microservices

A surrogate service can act as a replacement service if the main one fails.

Example:

If payment service fails

Another service acts as surrogate

3️⃣ In Real Life

Example: Surrogate Mother

A woman who carries a baby for another couple.

Quick Interview Definition

Surrogate Key:

A system-generated unique identifier used as the primary key that has no business meaning.